<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!--
  Airframe x500 (scripts/sim.sh --world x500): the model only; the world, sensors and specs as for sitl/airframes/x3.

  THE AIRCRAFT IS NOT INVENTED. Body, rotors, inertias, collisions, joints and motor constants are PX4's x500
  (PX4 airframe gz_x500, the Holybro X500 V2 in PX4's docs) from PX4-gazebo-models @ 155f58e (BSD-3):
  models/x500_base/model.sdf (base_link 2.0 kg, Ixx = Iyy 0.0216667, Izz 0.04; rotors 0.016077 kg at
  (+/-0.174, +/-0.174, 0.06) FLU) and models/x500/model.sdf (maxRotVelocity 1000, motorConstant 8.54858e-06,
  momentConstant 0.016, rotors 0, 1 ccw and 2, 3 cw -- the X3's order and spins, so the same Quad X allocation).
  Measured 2026-09-24 (world paused, rotor speeds set open-loop, odometry after N 1 ms steps): (850, 850, 750, 750)
  rad/s -> FLU angular z -0.202 rad/s at N 256 (nose right), (750, 750, 850, 850) -> +0.202; rotors 0, 2 at 850
  and 1, 3 at 800 -> FLU y -0.828 at N 128 (nose up: 0 and 2 are the front); 0, 3 at 850 -> FLU x -0.808 (right
  side up: 0 and 3 are the right). At rest the base link sinks 0.6 um in 2 s.
  The visual meshes are referenced as model://x500_base/..., resolved from airframe.json's mesh_path
  (~/sim/PX4-gazebo-models/models) when that checkout exists; without it the generator drops those visuals: the
  physics is unchanged and the viewer shows no body. Changes from PX4: the sensors are ours (fc3_sensors.sdf.in), not
  PX4's; <actuator_number> replaces the deprecated <motorNumber>; PX4's MotorFailurePlugin is not loaded; the model
  is named marv_quad (the bridge's topics carry it); the spawn height (airframe.json spawn_z) is 0.227 m, not PX4's
  0.24, so the landing-gear bars (base_link_collision_3/4, bottom at -0.2195 - 0.0075 m) rest on the ground rather
  than drop onto it.

  Take-off mass 2.0643 kg; full thrust 4 * 8.54858e-06 * 1000^2 = 34.19 N against 20.24 N of weight
  (thrust-to-weight 1.69), so hover sits at a thrust fraction of 0.592 (rotor speed fraction 0.769).
-->
